.TH ZERODDS-CORBA-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-corba-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-corba-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/corba-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the CORBA bridge daemon maps CORBA interface
operations onto DDS topics. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-corba-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the reader is
.I DaemonConfig::from_config
in
.IR crates/corba-dds-bridge/src/bridge_daemon/config.rs .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " corba ", " acl ", " mappings ", " tenants ", " metrics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr naming the key, then
starts; under
.B \-\-check\-config
it is an error. An unknown key inside a known section, or a value of the
wrong type, stops the start with file and line.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed. A
.B #
inside a quoted value is part of the value, not the start of a comment \(em a
.I corbaname
URL depends on that.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID of the daemon's participant. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS corba
.TP
.B orb_id
ORB identifier of this daemon.
.TP
.B idl_dir
The directory the IDL generated from the
.B idl_file
of the mappings is written to at start, one file per
.B idl_file
under its file name. Default
.IR /var/lib/zerodds/corba-bridge .
.TP
.B iiop
Sub-map with
.B bind
(listen address, e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:6833" ,
the default),
.B advertise_host
(the host the IORs name when
.B bind
is a wildcard address; default
.IR 127.0.0.1 ,
environment
.BR ZERODDS_CORBA_ADVERTISE_HOST ),
.B giop_version
.RI ( 1.0 " | " 1.1 " | " 1.2 ;
a mapped operation reached over 1.0 or 1.1 is answered NO_IMPLEMENT),
.B fragment_size
(replies above it go out in GIOP 1.2 and 1.1 fragments) and
.B max_message_size
(a larger inbound message is answered MessageError).
.TP
.B ssliop
Sub-map with
.BR enabled ", " bind ,
the server material
.BR cert_file " / " key_file ,
.B ca_file
(the server asks for a client certificate and checks one against it; its
subject DN, RFC 4514, and its fingerprint are the ACL subjects),
.B require_client_cert
(a session without a certificate fails; without it the session goes on
without a subject) and
.B required
(the objects are reached over SSLIOP only: the IORs name IIOP port 0, and the
plain IIOP listener answers a LocateRequest with OBJECT_FORWARD and a
Request with LOCATION_FORWARD to that IOR; needs
.BR enabled ).
.TP
.B ior
Sub-map with
.B ior_file
(one line per mapping:
.IR "repo_id operation IOR:..." ,
a tenant's as
.IR "@tenant repo_id operation IOR:..." ),
.B naming_service
(a
.IR corbaname: ", " corbaloc: " or " rir:
URL, CORBA 3.4 Part 2 \(sc13.6.10, over
.I iiop:
or
.IR ssliop: / tls: ),
.B publish_to_naming
(boolean: rebinds every receiving mapping's IOR into
.B naming_service
at start, under
.I <corbaname-fragment-path>/<repo_id-operation slug>
\(em every missing intermediate context in the path is created;
.I unbind
at a clean stop, before the drain; requires
.BR naming_service ),
.B naming_retry_ms
(total retry budget against
.BR naming_service ,
exponential backoff from 200\ ms capped at 5\ s; default
.IR 30000 ,
matching this daemon's own shutdown drain and its packaged unit's
.BR TimeoutStopSec ),
.B naming_ssliop
(for a NameService on
.IR ssliop: / tls: :
.B ca_file
its certificate is checked against, and
.BR cert_file " / " key_file
of this daemon when it asks for one) and
.B initial_references
(a map from a name to the
.IR corbaname: / corbaloc:
URL a
.I rir:
URL of that name resolves to, as
.I \-ORBInitRef
does for other ORBs).
.TP
.B naming
Sub-map with
.B serve
(host a
.I zerodds-corba-cosnaming
NamingContext, object key
.IR NameService ,
on this daemon's own IIOP/SSLIOP listener, the servant of
.BR zerodds-naming-svc (1))
and
.B persist_file
(its graph is loaded from here at start and saved after every change and at
the stop; empty: in memory).
.TP
.B csiv2
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean: every request's SAS
.I EstablishContext
is evaluated; a rejected one is
.B NO_PERMISSION
with a SAS
.B ContextError
attached, and so is a request with neither GSSUP credentials nor a verified
client certificate; the IOR carries
.B TAG_CSI_SEC_MECH_LIST
with a mechanism over TLS and one over plain IIOP),
.B target_supports
(list of accepted
.I IdentityToken
forms for CSIv2 identity assertion, Spec \(sc24.2.5: any of
.IR anonymous ", " principal_name ", " x509_cert_chain ", " distinguished_name ;
an asserted identity of an unlisted form is refused, and so is one other
than the authenticated GSSUP user itself or the anonymous identity) and
.BR gssup ,
a sub-map with
.B password_file
(a GSSUP credential file:
.I username:salt_hex:iterations:hash_hex
per line, PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256 \(em no plain-text password anywhere in this
daemon's configuration; required when
.B enabled
is true) and
.B target_name
(the AS-context target name the IOR advertises).
A CSIv2-accepted identity is added to the ACL's subjects as
.IR gssup:<username> ,
or, for an accepted identity assertion, the asserted name verbatim.
.SS acl
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean: without a rule for the caller, NO_PERMISSION.
.TP
.B rules
List of maps with
.B subject
.RI ( * ,
the client certificate's subject DN such as
.IR CN=trader,O=Example ,
its fingerprint
.IR mtls:<SHA-256 hex> ,
or
.IR gssup:<username> )
and
.BR allow_invoke ,
repository ids, a trailing
.I *
matching a prefix.
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9096"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
.TP
.B path
Only
.IR /metrics .
.SS mappings (list)
Each entry binds one CORBA operation to DDS topics.
.TP
.B repo_id
CORBA repository ID of the interface, e.g.
.IR "IDL:fin/PortfolioPublisher:1.0" .
.TP
.B operation
Operation name on that interface.
.TP
.B direction
.IR corba_to_dds " | " dds_to_corba " | " bidir .
.TP
.B request_topic
Sub-map carrying
.B dds_name
and
.BR dds_type ;
by default derived from repo_id and operation (\(sc5.1).
.TP
.B reply_topic
Sub-map as request_topic.
.TP
.B notify_topic
Sub-map as request_topic, for dds_to_corba.
.TP
.B correlation_id
The name of the first member of the request and reply types, which the
bridge fills. Default
.IR request_id ;
another name needs
.BR idl_file .
.TP
.B idl_file
The IDL of the interface (Spec \(sc5.2). The daemon looks up the operation
in the interface of
.B repo_id
(an attribute as
.IR _get_<name> " and " _set_<name> )
and generates the types
.IR <Interface>::<operation>::Request ", " Reply " and " Notify ,
which are then the types of the topics;
.B dds_type
beside it is refused. A user exception is a variant of the reply type by
its
.IR exception_kind ;
the daemon writes the GIOP exception from it. An operation with
.IR wchar ", " wstring ", " fixed ", " any ,
an object reference or a valuetype is refused at start.
.TP
.B timeout_ms
Reply wait; without a reply by then the caller gets TIMEOUT.
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map with
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ;
request-reply needs reliable),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local ;
with transient_local the replies are kept per request, and a request whose
reply is kept is answered from it),
.B history
(sub-map with
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last " | " keep_all )
and
.BR depth :
how many kept replies; keep_all with transient_local needs
.BR lifespan_ms ),
.B lifespan_ms
(of the request and notify samples and of a kept reply),
.B deadline_ms
(offered by the request writer, requested by the reply and notify readers; a
reply topic without a sample for that long answers the requests that waited
that long with TRANSIENT),
.B liveliness_lease_ms
(the lease of the DDS endpoints) and
.B partition
(list: the partitions of the DDS endpoints).
.TP
.B targets
For dds_to_corba: corbaloc URLs or stringified IORs every notify sample is
sent to as a oneway request.
.TP
.B target_object_keys
Not accepted: an object key names no host. The key stops the start with
that reason; list the targets as corbaloc URLs or IORs in
.BR targets .
.SS tenants (list)
Participants beside the one of
.B domain
(Spec \(sc1 L6). Each entry is a DDS participant of its own with
.B name
(in the IOR lines, the log, the spans and the metrics),
.B domain
(its DDS domain),
.B subjects
(the client certificates bound to it: a subject DN or
.IR mtls:<SHA-256 hex> ;
an SSLIOP session whose certificate names one is served by this tenant for
its life) and
.B mappings
(as above). Plain IIOP and every other session are the participant of
.BR domain .
A subject is bound to one tenant at most.
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/corba-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-corba-bridged (1).
